"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_5400995\", title: \"Prediction Fairness with respect to Sensitive Networks\", abstract: \"Algorithmic fairness is an important axis of ethical AI . We propose a novel approach to assess and mitigate the unfairness of classification models with respect to a given sensitive networks , such as social networks or professional networks . In this context , the fairness of a model correspond to the absence of correlation between the model predictions and the existence / absence of relations in a given sensitive networks , such as social networks or professional networks . We formalize criteria based on known concepts of group fairness using the assortativity coefficient , and We derive a regularization framework to mitigate the unfairness of a supervised model . Preliminary experiments on real-world case studies suggests that a regularization framework to mitigate the unfairness of a supervised model can be useful to explore the trade-off between accuracy and fairness . However , the use of GNN architectures may be required to find good compromises .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
