"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_5020362\", title: \"Foundation Model ColorMap : A Framework for Extracting and Visualizing the Foundation Models\u2019 Color Knowledge\", abstract: \"Recent advancements in AI have led to the development of powerful models capable of processing text , images , and multimodal data . These models , often referred to as \u201c foundation models , \u201d include Large Language Models ( LLMs ) and Visual Question Answering ( VQA ) systems . To evaluate These models , often referred to as \u201c foundation models , \u201d capabilities , benchmarks using stimulus-response paradigms have been designed to test performance across various domains . But researchers have not thoroughly tested color knowledge . Given the role of color in data visualization and the increasing integration of natural language interaction in applications , it is essential to investigate how These models , often referred to as \u201c foundation models , \u201d understand and represent color . The proposed framework systematically extracts and visualizes models \u2019 internal representations of color names . The proposed framework comprises two key components : a structured probing protocol and a visualization technique that maps color understanding . The proposed framework applies to Large Language Models ( LLMs ) through text-based analysis and to vision models via image-to-text processing . By comparing different models , we can assess different models conceptual integration of color .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
