children and adolescents , known as \u201c Programme d\u2019Aide Num\u00e9rique aux Devoirs pour Enfant avec TDA-H \u201d ( PANDAH ) for 3 months only ; and ( 3 ) adherence to our digital homework support program for children and adolescents , known as \u201c Programme d\u2019Aide Num\u00e9rique aux Devoirs pour Enfant avec TDA-H \u201d ( PANDAH ) , measured with in-app metrics . Results Recruitment began in January 2024 , and our ongoing randomized controlled trial is ongoing . Conclusions our ongoing randomized controlled trial contributes to the digital transformation of health care . The use of smartphone apps in self-care and self-management is a societal phenomenon , and The use of smartphone apps in self-care and self-management implementation in the field of psychiatry is of particular interest . The app might serve as both valuable support for patients and an opportunity for parents to distance parents from conflict-laden homework sessions . Since the market for smartphone apps in the health care and well-being sector is primarily industry driven , it is crucial to have an academic conception and evaluation of such digital tools . Trial Registration ClinicalTrials.gov NCT04857788 ; [ URL ] International Registered Report Identifier ( IRRID ) PRR1-10.2196/44553\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
