"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_5252288\", title: \"Revisiting Optimal Window Aggregation in Data Streams : The Prefix-Sum Approach\", abstract: \"The article presents a simple yet optimal approach to compute aggregates of window queries over data streams . a simple yet optimal approach to compute aggregates of window queries over data streams is built as a fully-fledged pipeline of operators that are literal transcripts of mathematical definitions . Main features are an application of the prefix sums and a well-founded un-/slicing technique . The overall process is linear in the number of events and windows , and The overall process takes quasi-constant space for a mix of periodic windows , still applicable to multiple deterministic window queries . The limitations are twofold : the events come in-order and the aggregation function is a left-cancellative monoid .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
