"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4654407\", title: \"Precedability Prediction Between Open Educational Resources\", abstract: \"The abundance of Educational Resources ( ERs ) has allowed people to have access to a vast amount of knowledge . However , it can be difficult , for both educators and learners , to navigate through Educational Resources ( ERs ) . One way to facilitate navigation is to identify useful relations between Educational Resources ( ERs ) . identify can improve the teaching and learning experiences by allowing the users to go from one resource to another based on the identified relations , such as precedence . In this work , we introduce the notion of precedability between educational resources ; whether a resource A can precede another resource B. Then , we propose a two-step method to identify precedability relations between educational resources . a two-step method to identify precedability relations between educational resources structures educational resources in an enriched Knowledge Graph ( KG ) . Then , a two-step method to identify precedability relations between educational resources uses a Graph Neural Network ( GNN ) model to predict precedability relations . a two-step method to identify precedability relations between educational resources performed better than multiple baselines on different benchmarks .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
