"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4213807\", title: \"A Hybrid Linear-Nonlinear ARX Model for reliable Multi-Step Prediction: application to SwPool Benchmark\", abstract: \"We present a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models . We motivation is to combine the advantages of linear and nonlinear models in the context of extrapolation outside of the training dataset . a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models uses a residual hybridization approach to ensure a large linear contribution . Based on a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models , a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models is evaluated using the available operating data of a specific aquatic center . The results obtained on this benchmark are compared to those of traditional linear and nonlinear identification , showing that a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models achieves both the accuracy of the pure nonlinear model and the consistency of the linear ARX model . a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models provides a promising solution for nonlinear identification , particularly for dynamical systems partially explainable by a linear model . As in the strictly linear case , a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models can be learned from a small volume of data , but can be enriched to improve prediction accuracy . a hybrid ARX model that is useful for system identification of nonlinear models potential use for data-based predictive control is particularly useful .\", labels: [\"Monitoring and Analysis\", \"Industrial Digitalization\", \"Digital Engineering of Products and Processes\", \"Industrial Organization Performance\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
