"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4106779\", title: \"Collaboration, Preservation and Sustainability in Digital Humanities: a question of time\", abstract: \"This paper discusses interdisciplinary collaborative practices based on the AdA project ( meaning \u201c Affektrhetoriken des Audiovisuellen \u201d [ URL ] in which institutionally situated research groups from computational sciences and film studies developed approaches for the analysis of the temporal dynamics of audiovisual expressivity by bringing together a theoretically informed methodology of film analysis and computational video analysis and semantic video annotation . In an earlier publication , we already presented how co-building a Digital Humanities tool could be seen as instrumental genesis . In an earlier publication we concentrated on the iterative development of a visualisation framework to highlight the need for a common language and for the consideration of time needed for collaboration . we would like to pursue the reflection on the instrumental genesis ( Rabardel , 1995 ) of collaboration tools along the time dimension . we saw that every step of tool development for such qualitative and exploratory research requires time : may time be for tool sketching , development , testing , or documenting tool usage for manual annotation .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
