"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4086508\", title: \"Operating data of a specific Aquatic Center as a Benchmark for dynamic model learning: search for a valid prediction model over an 8-hour horizon\", abstract: \"This article presents an identification benchmark based on data from a public swimming pool in operation . Such a system is both a complex process and easily understandable by all with regard to the stakes . Ultimately , the objective is to reduce the energy bill while maintaining the level of quality of service . the objective is general in scope and is not limited to public swimming pools . the objective can be done effectively through what is known as economic predictive control . economic predictive control is based on a process model . It is the aim of This article and an identification benchmark based on data from a public swimming pool in operation to show that such a dynamic model can be obtained from operating data . For obtained , operational data is formatted and shared , and model quality indicators are proposed . On this basis , the first identification results illustrate the results obtained by a linear multivariable model on the one hand , and by a neural dynamic model on the other hand . an identification benchmark based on data from a public swimming pool in operation calls for other proposals and results from control and data scientists for comparison .\", labels: [\"Monitoring and Analysis\", \"Eco-responsible Processes\", \"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
"MATCH (s:Entity { id: \"Entity_identification_benchmark\" }) MATCH (o:Article { id: \"Article_4086508\" }) MERGE (s)-[:APPEARS_IN]->(o);"
"MERGE (e:Entity {id: \"Entity_public_swimming_pool\", name: \"public_swimming_pool\"});"
