"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4083055\", title: \"Designing LADs That\u00a0Promote Sensemaking: A Participatory Tool\", abstract: \"Learning Analytics Dashboards ( LADs ) are data visualization tools built to empower teachers and learners to make purposeful decisions that impact the learning process . Due to Learning Analytics Dashboards ( LADs ) relatively recent emergence and the scarcity of studies on Learning Analytics Dashboards ( LADs ) design principles , Learning Analytics Dashboards ( LADs ) design remains a major area of investigation in learning analytics research , and large scale diffusion to Learning Analytics Dashboards ( LADs ) stakeholders remains limited . We promote human-centered approaches for LADs design since LADs success in terms of acceptance and adoption greatly depends on the level of stakeholder involvement in LADs design . In this paper , We present a tool to support the participatory design of LADs . First experiments during a pilot study with teachers demonstrate that a tool to support the participatory design of LADs encourages group work , and in-depth exploration of LADs use .\", labels: [\"Change Management\", \"User-Centered Design\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
