iously belong to multiple categories depending either on the multidimensional perception Seventy-seven odours and 26 categories are suggesting or on a conceptual positioning . the odour set is fully encoded into an rdf / owl Knowledge Graph , a semantic web standard language , which can be easily edited , stored , shared and requested . A hierarchical visual representation is derived to get a friendly and readable representation . The flexibility introduced by A hierarchical visual representation enables to easily find out the relevant term(s ) needed to describe an odorant perception . This approach , applied to food application , can be expanded to non-food sectors such as odour environment for example . SketchOscent is freely and publicly available at [ URL ]\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
