"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4374814\", title: \"Slicing techniques for temporal aggregation in spanning event streams\", abstract: \"Slicing is a popular approach to perform aggregation in streaming systems . Slicing allows sharing computation costs among overlapping windows . However streaming systems are limited to point events . In this paper , we address the temporal aggregate computation issue in streams where events come with a duration , denoted as spanning event streams . After a short review of the new constraints ensued by event lifespan in a temporal sliding-window context , we propose a new structure for dealing with slices in such an environment , and prove that we technique is both correct and effective to deal with such spanning events . we then further extend our technique to compensate for the new constraints induced by the duration of spanning events with a multi-level structure able to reduce insertion costs .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
