"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_3502370\", title: \"A 3-phase approach based on sequential mining and dependency parsing for enhancing hypernym patterns performance\", abstract: \"Abstract Patterns have been extensively used to extract hypernym relations from texts . The most popular patterns are Hearst \u2019s patterns , formulated as regular expressions mainly based on lexical information . Experiences have reported good precision and low recall for such patterns . Thus , several approaches have been developed for improving recall . While several approaches perform better in terms of recall , it remains quite difficult to further increase recall without degrading precision . In this paper , we propose a novel 3-phase approach based on sequential pattern mining to improve pattern-based approaches in terms of both precision and recall by ( i ) using a rich pattern representation based on grammatical dependencies ( ii ) discovering new hypernym patterns , and ( iii ) extending hypernym patterns with anti-hypernym patterns to prune wrong extracted hypernym relations . The results obtained by performing experiments on three corpora confirm that using a novel 3-phase approach based on sequential pattern mining to improve pattern-based approaches in terms of both precision and recall , we are able to learn sequential patterns and combine sequential patterns to outperform existing hypernym patterns in terms of precision and recall . The comparison to unsupervised distributional baselines for hypernym detection shows that , as expected , a novel 3-phase approach based on sequential pattern mining to improve pattern-based approaches in terms of both precision and recall yields much better performance . When compared to supervised distributional baselines for hypernym detection , a novel 3-phase approach based on sequential pattern mining to improve pattern-based approaches in terms of both precision and recall can be shown to be complementary and much less loosely coupled with training datasets and corpora .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
"MATCH (s:Entity { id: \"Entity_abstract_patterns\" }) MATCH (o:Article { id: \"Article_3502370\" }) MERGE (s)-[:APPEARS_IN]->(o);"
"MERGE (e:Entity {id: \"Entity_hypernym_relations\", name: \"hypernym_relations\"});"
