"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4106713\", title: \"Decision Support to Crowdsourcing for Annotation and Transcription of Ancient Documents: The RECITAL Workshop\", abstract: \"In the 18th century in Paris , only two public theatres could officially perform comedies : the Com\u00e9die-Fran\u00e7aise , and the Com\u00e9die-Italienne . the Com\u00e9die-Italienne was much less well known . By studying a century of accounting registers , we aim to learn more about a century of accounting registers successful plays , a century of accounting registers actors , musicians , set designers , and all the small trades necessary for a century of accounting registers operation , a century of accounting registers administration , logistics and finances . To aim , we employ a mass of untapped and unpublished resources , the 27,544 pages of 63 daily registers available at the Biblioth\u00e8que Nationale de France ( BnF ) . And we take a decidedly fresh look at emerging forms of creation and changes in the entertainment economy . we developed the crowdsourcing platform RECITAL to collect and index the data from a century of accounting registers , following an emerging trend in Digital Humanities . the crowdsourcing platform RECITAL is built upon the ScribeAPI framework and the crowdsourcing platform RECITAL offers a fully-fledged web application to classify the pages , annotate with marks and tags , transcribe the indexed marks and even to verify the previous transcripts . we also describe a multi-level data model and to develop a series of monitoring and decision tools to support crowdsourced data management up to their definitive form .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
