"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_3403131\", title: \"Temporal Aggregation of Spanning Event Stream: An Extended Framework to\u00a0Handle the Many Stream Models\", abstract: \"The Big Data era requires new processing architectures , among which streaming systems which have become very popular . streaming systems which are able to summarize infinite data streams with aggregates on the most recent data . However , up to now , only point events have been considered and spanning events , which come with a duration , have been let aside , restricted to the persistent databases world only . In this paper , we propose a unified framework to deal with such stream mechanisms on spanning events . To this end , we formally define a spanning event stream with new stream semantics and events properties , particularly considering how the event is received . we then review and extend usual stream windows to meet the new spanning event requirements . Eventually , we validate the soundness of a unified framework to deal with such stream mechanisms on spanning events with a set of experiments , based on a straightforward implementation , showing that aggregation of spanning event stream is providing as much new insight on the data as effectiveness in several use cases .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
