"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_4175668\", title: \"Incremental discovery of new defects: application to screwing process monitoring\", abstract: \"Defect detection by in-process monitoring plays a key role in the traceability and optimization of production . Many fault detection algorithms are trained on known faults . However , industrial data is generally unlabeled and certain faults are unknown or missing in the training dataset . This paper presents an original approach for the incremental discovery of new manufacturing defects , by Bayes rule and distance rejection . Rejects are analyzed periodically to determine the possible appearance of new defect cluster among Rejects . Visualization then supports the cluster interpretation by a manufacturing expert . an original approach for the incremental discovery of new manufacturing defects , by Bayes rule and distance rejection was successfully applied to a screwing database from automotive industry .\", labels: [\"Processes and Assembly\", \"Monitoring and Analysis\", \"Industrial Digitalization\", \"Industrial Organization Performance\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
"MATCH (s:Entity { id: \"Entity_defect_detection\" }) MATCH (o:Article { id: \"Article_4175668\" }) MERGE (s)-[:APPEARS_IN]->(o);"
