"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_2947879\", title: \"Window-Slicing Techniques Extended to Spanning-Event Streams\", abstract: \"Streaming systems often use slices to share computation costs among overlapping windows . However Streaming systems are limited to instantaneous events where only one point represents the event . Here , we extend streams to events that come with a duration , denoted as spanning events . After a short review of the new constraints ensued by event lifespan in a temporal sliding-window context , we propose a new structure for dealing with slices in such an environment , and prove that we technique is both correct and effective to deal with such spanning events . 2012 ACM Subject Classification Information systems \u2192 Stream management\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
