"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_2937636\", title: \"Temporal Aggregation of Spanning Event Stream: A General Framework\", abstract: \"The Big Data era requires new processing architectures among which the stream systems that have become very popular . the stream systems are able to summarize infinite data streams with aggregates on the most recent data . However , up to now , only point events have been considered and spanning events , which come with a duration , have been let aside , restricted to the persistent databases world only . In this paper , we propose an unified framework to deal with such stream mechanisms on spanning events . To this end , we formally define a spanning event stream with new stream semantics and events properties . we then review and extend usual stream windows to meet the new spanning events requirements . Eventually , we validate the soundness of an unified framework to deal with such stream mechanisms on spanning events with a set of experiments , based on a straightforward implementation , showing that aggregation of spanning event stream is providing as much new insights on the data as effectiveness in several use cases .\", labels: [\"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
