"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_3782708\", title: \"Leveraging Learners\u2019 Activity Logs for Course Reading Analytics Using Session-Based Indicators\", abstract: \"A challenge that course authors face when reviewing course authors contents is to detect how to improve course authors courses in order to meet the expectations of course authors learners . rnIn this paper , we propose an analytical approach that exploits learners ' logs of reading to provide authors with insightful data about the consumption of authors courses . we first model reading activity using the concept of reading-session and propose a new and efficient session identification . we then elaborate a list of indicators computed using learners ' reading sessions that allow to represent learners ' behaviour and to infer learners ' needs . we evaluate we proposals with course authors and learners using logs from a major e-learning platform . Interesting results were found . Interesting results demonstrates the effectiveness of an analytical approach that exploits learners ' logs of reading to provide authors with insightful data about the consumption of their courses in identifying aspects and parts of a course that may prevent a course from being easily read and understood , and for guiding the authors through the analysis and review tasks .\", labels: [\"User-Centered Design\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
