"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_3180284\", title: \"Metric learning for structured data\", abstract: \"Metric learning is a branch of machine learning , and more specifically representation learning , which involves learning the parameters of a metric in order to improve a metric intrinsic qualities when using a metric . In this thesis , we summarize recent developments around metric learning , both on so-called flat data , but also on structured data . The lack of power of representation of the metrics currently used leads we to propose a new metric based on sub-modular functions . a new metric based on sub-modular functions significantly increases the evaluation of interactions between data dimensions . A learning algorithm for a new metric based on sub-modular functions is then proposed . Secondly , we present two approaches LSCS ( selection of relational constraints ) and MRML ( multi-relation metric learning ) allowing to process types of data extremely present in information systems : relational databases . All of these proposals are then compared experimentally with existing ones , justifying the practical interest of All of these proposals .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
