"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_1874721\", title: \"Computational design of light and strong high entropy alloys (HEA) Obtainment of an extremely high specific solid solution hardening\", abstract: \"A multi-objective optimisation genetic algorithm combining solid solution hardening ( SSH ) and thermodynamic modelling ( CALPHAD ) with data mining is used to design high entropy alloys ( HEAs ) . A multi-objective optimisation genetic algorithm combining solid solution hardening ( SSH ) and thermodynamic modelling ( CALPHAD ) with data mining searches for the best compromise between single-phase stability , SSH and density . Thousands of Pareto-optimal base-centred cubic ( BCC ) HEAs are designed . Al35Cr35Mn8Mo5Ti17 ( at.% ) is chosen for experimental validation . The alloy was cast and characterised . The alloy microstructure consists of large grains of a single disordered solid solution displaying a Vickers hardness of 6.45 GPa ( 658 HV ) and a density below 5.5 g / cm3 ; uniquely combining exceptional hardness with medium density . \u00a9 2018 Acta Materialia Inc\", labels: [\"Composites and New Materials\", \"Industrial Digitalization\", \"Digital Engineering of Products and Processes\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
