"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_1912333\", title: \"Progressive sequential pattern mining: steerable visual exploration of patterns with PPMT\", abstract: \"The progressive visual analytics ( PVA ) paradigm has been proposed to describe visual analytics systems whose main goal is to reach a thorough coupling between the analyst and the analyst system by getting rid of waiting periods classically encountered during data process-ing . PVA systems use algorithms that both provide intermediate results throughout their execution , and are steerable by the analyst to change the strategy used to perform the remaining computation . Our focus is on progressive sequential pattern mining , as in the seminal work of Stolper et al . [ 30 ] . Here Our go further mainly by considering the temporal nature of patterns related to patterns occur-rences . Our propose a pattern-oriented data model , a pattern analysis task model , and guidelines for designing progressive pattern min-ing algorithms . Our introduce PPMT , a tool to support an analyst progressively explore activity traces , based on a modification of the GSP algorithm . Our evaluate proposed on the technical perfor-mances of Our progressive algorithm , and on the effect of steering on analysts \u2019 performances .\", labels: [\"Monitoring and Analysis\", \"Industrial Digitalization\"], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
"MATCH (s:Entity { id: \"Entity_progressive_visual_analytics\" }) MATCH (o:Article { id: \"Article_1912333\" }) MERGE (s)-[:APPEARS_IN]->(o);"
