"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_1982937\", title: \"Comparing of Term Clustering Frameworks for Modular Ontology Learning\", abstract: \"This paper aims to use term clustering to build a modular ontology according to core ontology from domain-specific text . The acquisition of semantic knowledge focuses on noun phrase appearing with the same syntactic roles in relation to a verb or a verb preposition combination in a sentence . The construction of this co-occurrence matrix from context helps to build feature space of noun phrases , which is then transformed to several encoding representations including feature selection and dimensionality reduction . In addition , the content has also been presented with the construction of word vectors . several encoding representations including feature selection and dimensionality reduction are clustered respectively with K-Means and Affinity Propagation ( AP ) methods , which differentiate into the term clustering frameworks . Due to the randomness of K-Means , iteration efforts are adopted to find the optimal parameter . the term clustering frameworks are evaluated extensively where AP shows dominant effectiveness for co-occurred terms and NMF encoding technique is salient by NMF encoding technique promising facilities in feature compression .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
