"MERGE (e:Article {id: \"Article_2156039\", title: \"A composite score associated with spontaneous operational tolerance in kidney transplant recipients\", abstract: \"New challenges in renal transplantation include using biological information to devise a useful clinical test for discerning high-and low-risk patients for individual therapy and ascertaining the best combination and appropriate dosages of drugs . Based on a 20-gene signature from a microarray meta-analysis performed on 46 operationally tolerant patients and 266 renal transplant recipients with stable function , we applied the sparse Bolasso methodology to identify a minimal and robust combination of six genes and two demographic parameters associated with operational tolerance . a minimal and robust combination of six genes and two demographic parameters associated with operational tolerance discriminated operationally tolerant patients with an area under the curve of 0.97 ( 95 % confidence interval 0.94-1.00 ) . a minimal and robust combination of six genes and two demographic parameters associated with operational tolerance was not influenced by immunosuppressive treatment , center of origin , donor type , or post-transplant lymphoproliferative disorder history of operationally tolerant patients . a minimal and robust combination of six genes and two demographic parameters associated with operational tolerance was significantly associated with both de novo anti-HLA antibodies and tolerance loss . a minimal and robust combination of six genes and two demographic parameters associated with operational tolerance was validated by quantitative polymerase chain reaction using independent samples and demonstrated specificity toward a model of tolerance induction . Thus , we score would allow clinicians to improve follow-up of patients , paving the way for individual therapy .\", labels: [], teams: [\"LS2N-DUKE\"]});"
"MATCH (s:Entity { id: \"Entity_clinical_test\" }) MATCH (o:Article { id: \"Article_2156039\" }) MERGE (s)-[:APPEARS_IN]->(o);"
